    answer:
      '<p><a href="https://onlinelibrary. Wiley. Com/doi/abs/10.1002/ejsp.674" target="_blank" rel="nofollow">Research says eighteen to two fifty-four days with an average of sixty-six days</a> according to University College London habit formation studies. Week one through two requires conscious effort and willpower. Week three through eight gets easier but still needs intention. Month three plus becomes more automatic. Faster adoption: link new habits to existing ones, start small, track completion, don\'t break chain on weekends.</p>',
  },
